FCC Datamart - Fine-tune extraction logic of BDS ODD alerts dataset and generate a new dataset to obtain ODD closed alert generated in BDS
Required Functionality	
Background
 
Currently, FCC Data Mart consists of ODD Alert Mart derived from BDS. However the risk level associated with these alerts is sourced from Detica and not BDS, which are updated on weekly basis.
 
These alerts may not reflect the actual risk level at the time alert ingest into BDS.
 
In order to obtain the actual risk level at the time alert ingested into BDS, ITD to incorporate new fields "BDS_CDD_RISK" in CIS_ODD dataset.
 
 
Furthermore, alert status of the dataset is not up to date due to the dataset is monthly cut-off.
 
In order to perform analysis and validation on the ODD closed alerts, a new data mart is required as per the following requirements.
 
Additonal effort is required to validate the completeness of ODD alert data between Detica and BDS.
 
 
Cross reference: SMR 2023-4345, SMR 2024-3862, SMR 2025-0850, Circular BPM/CIS/25/001.
 
 
Requirement 1
 
1) Extract "BDS_CDD_RISK" information from BDS.
 
2) Perform validation on data field of "BDS_CDD_RISK" to match BDS UI display as per attachment.
 
3) The above extraction/enhancement shall include backdated data from January 2024.
 
 
Requirement 2
 
1) ITD to generate a new dataset under FCC_MART folder (AMLA application) in the SAS-warehouse source from BDS.  
 
2) The output shall be populated as shown in the Attachment I.
 
3) Generate a yearly dataset based on "APPROVE_DATE" and append on a weekly basis.
 
4) The generated dataset shall name as CIR_CLOSE_YYYY and save under FCC_MART folder in SAS-warehouse.
 
5) The above records shall stored for 2 years in SAS Data-Warehouse. 
 
 
Remarks
 
- The FCC_MART folder in the SAS data warehouse can only be accessed by SAS users from Financial Crime Compliance, Compliance Division.
 
- This enhancement is for data extraction only, no further impact on other operational system and logic.
 
- All the existing requirements for all the datasets stored in FCC_MART folder remain unchanged. 
 
